50,3,1,talk,Servas,,"We have four candidates: A, B, C, and D. Given the history of failure for broad tools, A and B look risky.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Candidate A seems to address the address issues @Ryuji mentioned, but will it cost too much in licenses?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Candidate D is for the field, but I found out the network is bad! It might not even work!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Candidate A solves the misrouted deliveries and the copying of records. It is the most logical choice.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Candidate B just drafts summaries; it doesn't fix the staffing shortage. Candidate A reduces the redundant queries.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Servas,,Candidate C is a narrow tool for skill transfer. It fits the pattern of what survives.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,But Candidate A fixes the actual errors in the logs. I think it's more urgent.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Sakura,,I like the idea of the Training Studio! It's fun and helpful!,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, ""fun"" is not a business case. Candidate A stops the daily loss of time.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Asuka,,Candidate A removes the need for clerks to ask for the same certificates. It's a logical win.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Servas,,"If we choose A, we must ensure it is not too broad to be maintained.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"If we use the software allowance and fixed-fee build, it might fit the budget.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"I still think D is cool, but if the internet is gone, it's just a fancy brick.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,Then we are in agreement that A addresses the most significant operational failures.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I agree. A is the only one that reduces the actual workload of the staff.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Servas,,Let us vote.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll go with A.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I'll vote for C!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,A.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Asuka,,A.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
